NOTE ON THE AUDIO AND MODEL LICENSES

This repository's own scripts and documentation are MIT licensed.

The model used for the results documented here is `drama3-small-IQ3_XXS.gguf`
from https://huggingface.co/pentacoxian-dev/drama3-small-GGUF, which is
licensed under the **Fish Audio Community License v1.0** -- NOT MIT. See
https://huggingface.co/pentacoxian-dev/drama3-small-GGUF/blob/main/LICENSE

That license permits free research and non-commercial use, and limited
commercial use below USD 500k annual revenue. Hosting it as a TTS or
voice-cloning service requires a separate license from Fish Audio.

The runtime is audio.cpp: https://github.com/0xShug0/audio.cpp (MIT).

The generated audio clips in `audio/` were produced using the repository
author's own voice as reference material, for the purpose of documenting
these technical results.
